  "id": "Compound::DB00454 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Pethidine, a centrally acting opioid, is shown to bind to Cyp2d6, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which in turn participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This pathway leads to the activation of Cyp2c19, suggesting a potential role for Pethidine in modulating the metabolism of arachidonic acid through Cyp2d6. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Pethidine may influence Cyp2c19 through a shared pathway involving Cyp2d6, which is involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. The binding of Pethidine to Cyp2d6 appears to be a critical step in this process, as it is consistently linked to the subsequent activation of Cyp2c19. The mechanisms suggest that Pethidine could alter the activity of Cyp2c19 by modulating the expression or function of Cyp2d6, potentially affecting the metabolism of arachidonic acid and other substrates. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Pethidine and Cyp2c19, emphasizing the role of Cyp2d6 as a central mediator in this relationship.",
